  "goodToKnow": "Der Kommunist (die Kommunistin) is a communist. It's a weak noun: den Kommunisten. Communism has German roots: Karl Marx, born in Trier, and Friedrich Engels wrote the Kommunistisches Manifest in 1848. The KPD (Communist Party of Germany) was banned in West Germany in 1956, while East Germany was ruled by the SED until 1989. Kommunistisch means communist. Der Kommunismus is communism."
